<!DOCTYPE html>
<!--
  The consent screen.

  Deliberately standalone rather than wrapped in ``main_template``. This page
  is rendered inside somebody else's login journey: the relying party sent the
  browser here and is waiting for it back, and a page that inherits the site's
  navigation invites the user to wander off mid-flow. It is a page template
  rather than a string built in Python so a site can restyle or override it,
  which the refusal page above it does not need to be: nobody themes an
  error that means the request was not trustworthy enough to redirect.
-->
<html xmlns:tal="http://xml.zope.org/namespaces/tal"
      lang="en"
>
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport"
          content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"
    />
    <meta name="robots"
          content="noindex, nofollow"
    />
    <title tal:content="string:Authorize ${view/client_title}">Authorize</title>
    <style>
      body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 0; padding: 2rem;
             background: #f4f4f5; color: #18181b; }
      main { max-width: 30rem; margin: 3rem auto; background: #fff;
             padding: 2rem; border-radius: .5rem;
             box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.1); }
      h1 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-top: 0; }
      ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; }
      li { margin-bottom: .25rem; }
      .actions { display: flex; gap: .75rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
      button { font: inherit; padding: .5rem 1.25rem; border-radius: .25rem;
               border: 1px solid #d4d4d8; cursor: pointer; }
      button.allow { background: #1e40af; border-color: #1e40af; color: #fff; }
      .who { color: #52525b; font-size: .875rem; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1 tal:content="string:Allow ${view/client_title} to use your account?">
        Allow this application to use your account?
      </h1>

      <p class="who">
        You are signed in as
        <strong tal:content="view/user_label">someone</strong>.
      </p>

      <div tal:condition="view/scope_list">
        <p>It is asking for:</p>
        <ul>
          <li tal:repeat="scope view/scope_list"
              tal:content="scope"
          >scope</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <p tal:condition="not:view/scope_list">
        It is not asking for any particular permission, only for a token that
        says who you are.
      </p>

      <form method="post"
            tal:attributes="
              action view/form_action;
            "
      >
        <!--
          Every parameter of the original request is posted back rather than
          held in a session. The authorization request belongs to the client
          rather than to this server, and re-reading it from the form on the
          way out means there is no server-side state to expire between the
          question and the answer.
        -->
        <input type="hidden"
               tal:repeat="field view/form_fields"
               tal:attributes="
                 name field/name;
                 value field/value;
               "
        />
        <input name="_authenticator"
               type="hidden"
               tal:attributes="
                 value view/authenticator_token;
               "
        />
        <div class="actions">
          <button class="allow"
                  name="consent"
                  type="submit"
                  value="allow"
          >
            Allow
          </button>
          <button name="consent"
                  type="submit"
                  value="deny"
          >
            Deny
          </button>
        </div>
      </form>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
